            <ArticleTitle>Two-vessel coronary artery dissection in the peripartum period. Case report and literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>809-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of early peripartum myocardial infarction resulting from spontaneous dissection of the left anterior descending coronary artery and right coronary artery in a twenty-four-year-old woman. This is the first report of double-vessel coronary dissection involving both the left and right coronary arteries diagnosed antemortem and successfully treated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
